section.p:
        Create an SComboBox and associate it with an ArrayList in the model, which will hold 
        the list of items that the SCombobox will contain. 

        The ArrayList is populated with value objects. In the model, create a getter method for 
        a specific instance of the member value objects, so that the model can be aware of which 
        object is selected in the view. 

        Below is an example of how to initially create the SComboBox: 

// In the view: 
  countryCombo = new SComboBox(); 
  // Set the selector to the ArrayList of items. 
  countryCombo.setSelector("countryList");
  // Set renderer selector to the field within the item model that you want to display. 
  countryCombo.setRendererSelector("countryName");
  // Set the selection selector to the item variable from the Item Model. 
  countryCombo.setSelectionSelector("selectedCountry");

// In the model
